steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∉ ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy returns (False, \"Tool '{tool}' is not recognized.'\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name ∈ ALLOWED_TOOLS AND tool_name ≠ HIGH_RISK_TOOL THEN policy returns (True, \"Tool '{tool}' is safe and allowed.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND any of {query_policy_result, verify_document_result, check_preexisting_condition_result, calculate_payout_result, amount} is missing THEN policy returns (False, \"Missing required arguments for approve_payout: ...\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND query_policy_result.status ≠ REQUIRED_POLICY_STATUS THEN policy returns (False, \"Policy status is '{status}', required '{REQUIRED_POLICY_STATUS}'.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND verify_document_result.authenticity ≠ REQUIRED_AUTHENTICITY THEN policy returns (False, \"Document authenticity is '{auth}', required '{REQUIRED_AUTHENTICITY}'.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND verify_document_result.authenticity ∈ {\"Low\", \"Medium\"} THEN policy returns (False, \"Document authenticity is low/medium; approve_payout not permitted.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND check_preexisting_condition_result.is_preexisting = true AND check_preexisting_condition_result.exclusion_applies = true THEN policy returns (False, \"Pre‑existing condition with exclusion applies; payout cannot be approved.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND amount > query_policy_result.coverage_limit THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested amount {amount} exceeds coverage limit {coverage_limit}.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND amount > (query_policy_result.claim_amount - query_policy_result.deductible) THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested amount {amount} exceeds claim amount after deductible ({max_after_deductible}).\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND amount > calculate_payout_result.suggested_payout THEN policy returns (False, \"Requested amount {amount} exceeds suggested payout {suggested_payout}.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND all required arguments are present AND query_policy_result.status = REQUIRED_POLICY_STATUS AND verify_document_result.authenticity = REQUIRED_AUTHENTICITY AND NOT (check_preexisting_condition_result.is_preexisting = true AND check_preexisting_condition_result.exclusion_applies = true) AND amount ≤ query_policy_result.coverage_limit AND amount ≤ (query_policy_result.claim_amount - query_policy_result.deductible) AND amount ≤ calculate_payout_result.suggested_payout THEN policy returns (True, \"approve_payout allowed: all prerequisite checks satisfied.\")"
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF tool_name = HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND any of the above allowed‑case conditions is false THEN policy returns (False, <specific reason describing the first failed check>)"
  }
]

**Rationale:**  
These IF‑THEN clauses capture every security requirement: they first filter out unrecognized tools, then grant unconditional access to all safe tools, and finally enforce the full set of prerequisite checks for the critical `approve_payout` action. Each clause ties a concrete precondition on the input arguments to the exact Boolean and message returned by the `policy` function, covering both permitted and denied scenarios, including the special cases of low document authenticity and excluded pre‑existing conditions. This makes the policy’s behavior fully auditable and mechanically verifiable.

[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ≠ 'approve_payout' THEN return (True, any) PROVIDED all parameters listed in REQUIRED_PARAMS[arguments.tool_name] are present."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND any of the parameters {claim_id, amount, query_policy_result, verify_document_result, check_preexisting_condition_result, calculate_payout_result} is missing THEN return (False, \"Missing required argument(s) for 'approve_payout'.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.query_policy_result.policy_status ≠ 'Active' THEN return (False, \"Policy status '{policy_status}' is not 'Active'.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.verify_document_result.authenticity ≠ 'High' THEN return (False, \"Document authenticity '{authenticity}' is not required 'High'.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.verify_document_result.authenticity ∈ {'Low','Medium'} THEN return (False, \"Document authenticity is insufficient; must call deny_claim, flag_fraud, or escalate_to_human.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.check_preexisting_condition_result.is_preexisting = true AND arguments.check_preexisting_condition_result.exclusion_applies = true THEN return (False, \"Pre‑existing condition with exclusion applies; must call deny_claim with reason.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.amount > arguments.query_policy_result.coverage_limit THEN return (False, \"Requested amount {amount} exceeds coverage limit {coverage_limit}.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.amount > max(0, arguments.query_policy_result.claim_amount - arguments.query_policy_result.deductible) THEN return (False, \"Requested amount {amount} exceeds claim amount after deductible ({max_allowed}).\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND arguments.amount > arguments.calculate_payout_result.suggested_payout THEN return (False, \"Requested amount {amount} exceeds suggested payout {suggested_payout}.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND all of the following hold: (1) query_policy_result.policy_status = 'Active', (2) verify_document_result.authenticity = 'High', (3) NOT (check_preexisting_condition_result.is_preexisting = true AND check_preexisting_condition_result.exclusion_applies = true), (4) amount ≤ query_policy_result.coverage_limit, (5) amount ≤ max(0, query_policy_result.claim_amount - query_policy_result.deductible), (6) amount ≤ calculate_payout_result.suggested_payout THEN return (True, \"approve_payout allowed: all prerequisite checks satisfied.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name = 'approve_payout' AND any prerequisite check fails THEN the agent MUST subsequently invoke exactly one of {deny_claim, flag_fraud, escalate_to_human} with a non‑empty reason where the policy requires it (e.g., pre‑existing‑condition exclusion)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments.tool_name ∈ {'deny_claim','flag_fraud','escalate_to_human'} AND required parameters for that tool are missing THEN return (False, \"Missing required argument(s) for '{tool_name}'.\")."
  }
]

These IF‑THEN clauses capture every precondition that must be satisfied before the high‑risk `approve_payout` tool can be executed, define the allowed fallback actions when any check fails, and confirm that all other tools are permitted as long as their required arguments are supplied.

